    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "chat",
        "title": "Format single-turn Dots and Ernie prompts without ChatML",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "`Dots1Model.default_chat_prompt` encloses a truthy system prompt in `<|system|>\u2026<|endofsystem|>`, wraps the user text in `<|userprompt|>\u2026<|endofuserprompt|>`, and ends at `<|response|>`. It inserts no whitespace. Both pinned Dots tokenizer templates use these delimiters, but the helper still omits the system block for a missing or empty system prompt. The base checkpoint emits an empty block when no system message is supplied; the instruction checkpoint inserts \u201cYou are a helpful assistant.\u201d",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_f8823f58596a4cce8c10dc2eb2f9dfb4",
              "call_2f49bfd69a574d46875feba6f395b6be",
              "call_92bea65e507240bba577fc0a08d58628"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "`Ernie4_5Model.default_chat_prompt` and `Ernie4_5MoEModel.default_chat_prompt` now build identical strings: `<|begin_of_sentence|>`, then truthy system text followed by a newline, then `User: ` plus the user text and a newline, then `Assistant: ` with its trailing space. That is the pending-turn form in the ERNIE-4.5-0.3B-PT, ERNIE-4.5-21B-A3B-PT and ERNIE-4.5-300B-A47B-PT templates with no system message or a nonempty one. An explicitly empty system message contributes a newline in those templates but not in the helper. The tokenizer metadata distinguishes the begin-of-sentence marker (`cls_token`) from BOS (`<s>`); the helper emits the former as text and does not add the latter as a token.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_27de021cf5f74b859c045d30c9b36b26",
              "call_a27ff80d77994795bb947f8d94919689",
              "call_55b5e30bb3214099b326685cf695f232",
              "call_3e98517d655d4746ba12d61829225135",
              "call_91214fed24d84b02b9babdb9a0e79fed"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library transcription compared the new strings against the corresponding single-turn template branches. With nonempty system text both families matched. With no system message, Ernie matched and Dots instruction did not. With an explicitly empty system message both differed. This checked text and whitespace, not token IDs.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_db5fe0011c994f5f9fbc4fec1cba107f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The pinned configs for `dots-studio/dots.llm1.base` and `dots-studio/dots.llm1.inst` each map to the same Dots text class: both specify width 4096, 32 query and KV heads, and 62 layers. Both use the head-width fallback and override the dense-prefix, shared-expert and selected-expert defaults. The formatter does not branch on these dimensions or on their different configured EOS IDs.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_1951b5e458f9497f9ba007860d66e851",
              "call_82215676ce714faa8766ac8dc26d65ff",
              "call_8f611d1d094c42819eea327ec125b261",
              "call_f8823f58596a4cce8c10dc2eb2f9dfb4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The pinned `baidu/ERNIE-4.5-0.3B-Base-PT`, `-Base-Paddle`, `-PT` and `-Paddle` configs each map to the dense class: width 1024, 16 query/two KV heads, 18 layers, explicit head width 128 rather than the fallback, and tied embeddings. None of those values is read by the formatter.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_2c9741df2da24384b892dc9f9355efbe",
              "call_26cb37df6c244f1397eb5ed1974900b2",
              "call_283f7f7b786d423ab4b78b35b9e24cf6",
              "call_e2afabdb4f794c3bad24ecd7c85ac185",
              "call_1f0bebf402584ef593ed84697f341d95",
              "call_27de021cf5f74b859c045d30c9b36b26"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The pinned `baidu/ERNIE-4.5-21B-A3B-Base-PT`, `-Base-Paddle`, `-PT` and `-Paddle` configs each map to the MoE class with width 2560, 20 query/four KV heads, 28 layers, one dense-prefix layer and two shared experts. The pinned `baidu/ERNIE-4.5-300B-A47B-2Bits-Paddle`, `-Base-PT`, `-Base-Paddle`, `-FP8-Paddle`, `-PT`, `-Paddle` and `-W4A8C8-TP4-Paddle` configs each map to that class with width 8192, 64 query/eight KV heads, 54 layers, three dense-prefix layers and the zero shared-expert default. All omit `head_dim` and use the same fallback rule. The MoE helper is independent of these values and does not add support for any format declared by the quantized configs.",
            "basis": "source",
